  "review_resolutions": [
    "ES3 indexed transform-feedback draw replaced with DrawArrays preserving input ID",
    "Unneeded arithmetic-interval acceptance removed completely; exact measured-query CPU winner required",
    "GPU-query transform and normal separately bounded against double reference",
    "Fusion cutoff evaluated once and shared by CPU, uniform and reporting; PointRemoval cutoff unchanged",
    "Invariant query outputs; desktop-only invariant matching inputs; both language rules checked in primary specifications",
    "NaN sentinel and exactly-one captured primitive check",
    "GPU query errors wrapped with original mismatch diagnostic; GL flags drained in setup and completion paths",
    "Execution failure remains visible until reset; stale previous failure file removed on construction/reset",
    "Final prose matches all four actual states; separate native/offline output paths prevent mixed-run evaluation",
    "Direct-run EGL vendor export distinguished from CTest CMake cache option"
  ],
  "limitations": [
    "One recorded scene;120 selected frames, not all798 original frames",
    "Supplied camera calibration and motion-capture poses; no tracking benchmark",
    "Fusion selections use read-back GPU index map; index rasterization/removal outputs not independently checked in native runs",
    "One Mac and one iOS record require bounded transformed GPU query followed by EXACT CPU winner; no selection tolerance or arithmetic-interval fallback",
    "Platform output counts differ; source-view rasterization and floating-point behavior can differ",
    "Held-out frames are interleaved nearby viewpoints of same noisy sensor/scene, not independent surface truth",
    "MAE/RMSE use different overlapping pixel subsets; raw union scores higher on coverage and within50mm over all valid pixels",
    "Actual screen clips are excerpts; iOS USB stream timing differs from wall time; no playback throughput claim"
  ],
